# QWEN_FAILOVER_GOVERNOR_ACCOUNTING_20260822.patch
# Contract patch / integration guidance. Do not apply blindly across a moving PR.
# Fresh preimage: qwen-free-api head 36dcf2424923de926e3e04848ae2e5dfa6402645.
#
# Required behavior:
#
# 1. Carry governor size metadata in the request-wide attempt context after the
#    initial preparePublicPayloadGoverned() admission:
#
#    requestAttemptContext.governorChars = <the exact admission chars>;
#    requestAttemptContext.governedAccountIds = new Set([preferredAccount.id]);
#    requestAttemptContext.settledGovernorAccountIds = new Set();
#
# 2. In qwen-client, immediately before first provider I/O on any sibling account
#    selected by sendChatRequest()/generateChatID(), ensure that account has its own
#    admission:
#
#    await ensureGovernorAdmission(attemptContext, account)
#
#    where ensureGovernorAdmission calls requestGovernor.before(account.id,
#    { chars: attemptContext.governorChars }) exactly once per account.
#
# 3. Before continuing from a failed account A to sibling B, settle A's admission
#    exactly once with the same classified failure that caused failover. Do this for
#    captcha/rate-limit/auth/transport branches that continue to another account.
#
# 4. Do NOT settle the final successful account inside qwen-client: keep that
#    admission until quota telemetry has actual usage, then success(finalAccount,
#    usage) settles it. Telemetry must know that earlier failed attempts were already
#    settled and must never emit a second outcome for them.
#
# 5. If the whole operation terminates before a final successful response, settle
#    the last admitted-but-unsettled account exactly once before returning the local
#    error. Local preparation failures before provider I/O must not be mislabeled as
#    provider pressure.
#
# Regression required before product write:
#   A admitted -> A CAPTCHA -> B admitted -> B succeeds -> response finishes
# Assertions:
#   admissions == [A, B]
#   outcomes include failure(A, captcha) and success(B, usage)
#   pending(A) == 0
#   pending(B) == 0
#   provider calls to B before before(B) == 0
#   failover budget/account affinity semantics unchanged
